<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khorat Plateau</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Isan Plateau, Isan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Khorat Plateau is a broad, low plateau in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, bounded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-river">Mekong</a> river to the north and east and by the Phetchabun and Dangrek ranges. It covers most of the Isan region, drained by the Mun and Chi rivers. Once dotted with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> temples such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phimai">Phimai</a>, it was long contested between Lao, Siamese and Khmer states, and its people are mostly Lao-speaking.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khorat-plateau.jpg" alt="Khorat Plateau" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Love Krittaya · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Farm_TH.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
